<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b65\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">M</forename><surname>Zhuge</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">W</forename><surname>Wang</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">L</forename><surname>Kirsch</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">F</forename><surname>Faccio</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">D</forename><surname>Khizbullin</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">J</forename><surname>Schmidhuber</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<idno type=\"arXiv\">arXiv:2402.16823</idno>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Language agents as optimizable graphs</title>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date type=\"published\" when=\"2024\">2024</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note type=\"report_type\">arXiv preprint</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b66\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">A</forename><surname>Zou</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">L</forename><surname>Phan</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">S</forename><surname>Chen</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">J</forename><surname>Campbell</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">P</forename><surname>Guo</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">R</forename><surname>Ren</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">A</forename><surname>Pan</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">X</forename><surname>Yin</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">M</forename><surname>Mazeika</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">A.-K</forename><surname>Dombrowski</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<idno type=\"arXiv\">arXiv:2310.01405</idno>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Representation engineering: A top-down approach to ai transparency</title>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date type=\"published\" when=\"2023\">2023</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note type=\"report_type\">arXiv preprint</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b67\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Study on Intermediate Error Tracking of LatentMAS Incorrect Case with LatentMAS (Debug Mode) Question: In a room, there are various toys: 5 red cars, 3 action figures, and a doll. The doll costs as much as 3 action figures and one red car costs 4 dollars. How much are all toys worth</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">I</forename><surname>Case</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>of an action figure costs 5 dollars? Planner: Okay, I need to make a detailed plan to solve the math problem</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b68\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Determine the cost of one action figure</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>given as $5</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b69\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Calculate the total cost of the doll; calculate the total cost of all red cars using the given cost of one red car ($4); calculate the total cost of all action figures by multiplying the number of action figures by the cost of one action figure</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b70\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">Add the costs of all toys (red cars, action figures, and the doll) to find the total value of all toys</title>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">The original plan from the Planner Agent was</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b71\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Identify the cost of action figure</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b72\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Calculate the total cost for each type by multiplying the quantity by the individual cost</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b73\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">But the doll&apos;s cost isn&apos;t given directly. It&apos;s given in terms of other toys. So, the first step should be to calculate the doll&apos;s cost based on the given relationship. The original plan might have missed that step, assuming that the cost of each type is given directly</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Sum up all the total costs to find the total value of all toys Let me check the original plan again But the problem is that the Planner Agent&apos;s plan didn&apos;t account for the doll&apos;s cost being dependent on the action figures and the red car. So, the original plan might have missed that step which is not the case for the doll. Therefore, the plan needs to be adjusted to first calculate the doll&apos;s cost using the given relationship before proceeding to calculate the total cost for each type</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b74\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">the feedback should point out that the plan didn&apos;t account for the doll&apos;s cost calculation based on the given relationship. The user needs to first determine the doll&apos;s cost by using the values of the action figures and the red car, then proceed with the rest of the steps</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Refiner: The Original Plan is</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b75\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Calculate the total cost for each type by multiplying the quantity by the individual cost</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b76\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Feedback: The original plan fails to explicitly address the doll&apos;s cost, which is not directly given but derived from the cost of 3 action figures and 1 red car. To refine the plan: • First, calculate the doll&apos;s cost using the given relationship (3 × action figure cost + 1 × red car cost)</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Sum up all the total costs to find the total value of all toys</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b77\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Ensure all quantities (5 red cars, 3 action figures, 1 doll) are accounted for</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b78\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Clarify that the total value includes all toys with their respective quantities and derived costs</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>The Refined Plan is</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b79\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Determine individual costs</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b80\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Solver: To determine the total value of all the toys, the doll costs as much as 3 action figures and 1 red car, so Doll = 3 • $5 + 1 • $4 = $19</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Sum all totals If Jan is 30 how old is Jean? Planner</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b81\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Determine Mark&apos;s current age by using the information about his age two years ago relative to Jan&apos;s age</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b82\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Calculate half of Jan&apos;s age two years ago and then determine Mark&apos;s age at that time based on the given relationship</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b83\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">The original plan provided by the Planner Agent was a bit incomplete, so I need to figure out where it went wrong. The original plan is a good start but lacks specific details on how to calculate Mark&apos;s age two years ago and how to derive Jean&apos;s age from Mark&apos;s current age. To improve, the plan should explicitly outline the mathematical operations needed, such as calculating half of Jan&apos;s current age, adding 5 years, adjusting for the two-year time difference, and then applying the age difference between Jean and Mark. Additionally, the plan should emphasize verifying each step for consistency with the given information. Refiner: First, I need to break down the information step by step. Let&apos;s start by noting down all the given information clearly. Jan&apos;s current age is 30</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Use the relationship between Jean and Mark&apos;s ages to find Jean&apos;s current age. Critic: The user wants to know Jean&apos;s age based on the given information That&apos;s a concrete number, so that&apos;s a good starting point</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b84\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">the problem mentions something about two years ago. So, I should probably calculate Jan&apos;s age two years ago. Since Jan is 30 now, two years ago she was 30 -2 = 28 years old</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>Next</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>That seems straightforward</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b85\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Then adding 5 years to that gives 14 + 5 = 19. So, Mark was 19 years old two years ago. Therefore, Mark&apos;s current age would be 19 + 2 = 21 years old. Wait, that seems a bit young</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>Now</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>the problem says that two years ago, Mark was 5 years older than half of Jan&apos;s age at that time. So, half of Jan&apos;s age two years ago is 28/2 = 14 but maybe that&apos;s correct based on the given info</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b86\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Adding 5 gives 19, which is Mark&apos;s age two years ago. Adding 2 years brings Mark&apos;s current age to 21. Jean is two years older than Mark, so 21+2 = 23. That seems consistent. Feedback: The original plan is a good start but lacks specific details on how to calculate Mark&apos;s age two years ago and how to derive Jean&apos;s age from Mark&apos;s current age. To improve, the plan should explicitly outline the mathematical operations needed, such as calculating half of Jan&apos;s current age</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>Then</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>the problem states that Jean is two years older than Mark If Mark is currently 21, then Jean would be 21 + 2 = 23 years old Let me verify each step again. Jan is 30 now. Two years ago, she was 28. Half of 28 is 14 But wait, that seems like a possible answer, but I need to check if I did all the steps correctly adding 5 years, adjusting for the two-year time difference, and then applying the age difference between Jean and Mark. Additionally, the plan should emphasize verifying each step for consistency with the given information. The Refined Plan is</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b87\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Identify known values</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b88\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Calculate Jan&apos;s age two years ago</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b89\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Determine Mark&apos;s age two years ago</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b90\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Calculate Mark&apos;s current age</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b91\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">According to the provided plan, to solve the problem step-by-step: Jan is currently 30, so two years ago Jan was 30 -2 = 28. Half of Jan&apos;s age two years ago is 28/2 = 14, and Mark was 5 years older than that at the time, so Mark was 14 + 5 = 19 two years ago and is therefore 19 + 2 = 21 now. Since Jean is 2 years older than Mark, Jean is 21 + 2 = 23 years old. Hence, the final answer is 23</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Find</forename><surname>Jean's Current Age</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>Solver</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Prompt Template for LatentMAS Sequential LatentMAS Prompts on Numeric Tasks (GSM8K / AIME2024 / AIME2025</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b92\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">System Prompt for All Agents: You are Qwen, created by Alibaba Cloud. You are a helpful assistant. Prompt for Planner Agent: You are a Planner Agent. Given an input question, design a clear, step-by-step plan for how to solve the question. Question: {question} Your outlined plan should be concise with a few bulletpoints for each step. Do not produce the final answer. Now output your plan to solve the question below: Prompt for Critic Agent: You are a Critic Agent to evaluate the correctness of the input plan for the given question and provide helpful feedback for improving the plan. Question: {question} The plan information is provided in latent KV representation format. Review the plan and question and output: (1) original plan contents (2) constructive feedback on the original plan. Format your response as follows: Original Plan: [Copy the provided Planner Agent&apos;s plan here] Feedback: [Your detailed feedback to improve the plan here] Now, output your response below: Prompt for Refiner Agent: You are a Refiner Agent to provide a refined step-by-step plan for solving the given question. Question: {question} You are provided with: (1) latent-format information: a previous plan with feedback (2) text-format information: the input question you need to solve. Based on the input, write a refined and improved plan to solve the question. Make sure your output plan is correct and concise. Now, output your refined plan below: Prompt for Solver Agent: You are a helpful assistant. You are provided with latent information for reference and a target question to solve. Target Question: {question} The latent information might contain irrelevant contents</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Arc-C</forename><surname>Arc-E</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Gpqa</forename><surname>Medqa</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">)</forename></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Prompt for Planner Agent: You are a Planner Agent</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>System Prompt for All Agents: You are Qwen Given an input question, design a clear step plan for how to solve the question Question: {question} Your outlined plan should be concise with a few bulletpoints for each step Question: {question} The plan information is provided in latent KV representation format Do not produce the final answer. Now output your plan to solve the question below: Prompt for Critic Agent: You are a Critic Agent to evaluate the correctness of the input plan for the given question and provide helpful feedback for improving the plan Review the plan and question and output: (1) original plan contents (2) constructive feedback on the original plan. Format your response as follows: Original Plan: [Copy the provided Planner Agent&apos;s plan here] Feedback: [Your detailed feedback to improve the plan here] Now, output your response below: Prompt for Refiner Agent: You are a Refiner Agent to provide a refined step-by-step plan for solving the given question. Question: {question} You are provided with: (1) latent-format information: a previous plan with feedback (2) text-format information: the input question you need to solve. Based on the input, write a refined and improved plan to solve the question. Make sure your output plan is correct and concise. Now, output your refined plan below: Prompt for Solver Agent: You are a helpful assistant. You are provided with latent information for reference and a target question to solve. Target Question: {question} The latent information might contain irrelevant contents. Ignore it if it is not helpful for solving the target question. Now, reason step by step and output the final answer inside \\boxed{YOUR FINAL ANSWER}: Sequential LatentMAS prompts for multiple-choice tasks Ignore it if it is not helpful for solving the target question. Your final answer must be selected from A,B,C,D. For example \\boxed{A}. Do not add any other contents inside the box. Now, reason step by step and output the final answer inside \\boxed{YOUR FINAL ANSWER}: Sequential LatentMAS prompts for python coding tasks (MBPP-Plus, HumanEval-Plus</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b93\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">Your must reason step-by-step to solve the **provided Target Question** witout outputing other irrelevant inforamtion. You must put all python code as self-contained Python function in markdown code blocks. For example &apos;&apos;&apos;python import math def add(a, b): return a + b&apos;&apos;&apos;. Do not add any other contents inside the markdown code block. Now, reason step by step and output the final answer inside &apos;&apos;&apos;python YOUR PYTHON CODE&apos;&apos;&apos;: Hierarchical LatentMAS prompts for numeric-answer tasks (GSM8K, AIME2024, AIME2025) System prompt for All Agents: You are Qwen, created by Alibaba Cloud. You are a helpful assistant. Prompt for Math Agent: You are a math agent. Given the input question, reason step-by-step and put the final answer inside \\boxed{YOUR FINAL ANSWER}. Question: {question} Your response: Prompt for Science Agent: You are a science agent. Given the input question, reason step-by-step and put the final answer inside \\boxed{YOUR FINAL ANSWER}. Question: {question} Your response: Prompt for Code Agent: You are a code agent. Given the input question, reason step-by-step and put the final answer inside \\boxed{YOUR FINAL ANSWER}. Question: {question} Your response: Prompt for Task Summarizer Agent: You are a task summarizer. Given the input question and responses from previous agents as reference, reason step-by-step and put the final answer inside \\boxed{YOUR FINAL ANSWER}. Question: {question} Your response: You are a code agent. Given the input question, reason step-by-step and put the final answer inside \\boxed{YOUR FINAL ANSWER}. Your final answer must be selected from A,B,C,D. For example \\boxed{A}. Do not add any other contents inside the box. Question: {question} Your response: Prompt for Task Summarizer Agent: You are a task summarizer. Given the input question and responses from previous agents as reference</title>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Prompt for Planner Agent: You are a Planner Agent</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>System Prompt for All Agents: You are Qwen Given an input question, design a clear step plan for how to solve the question Question: {question} Your outlined plan should be concise with a few bulletpoints for each step Question: {question} The plan information is provided in latent KV representation format Do not produce the final answer. Now output your plan to solve the question below: Prompt for Critic Agent: You are a Critic Agent to evaluate the correctness of the input plan for the given question and provide helpful feedback for improving the plan Review the plan and question and output: (1) original plan contents (2) constructive feedback on the original plan. Format your response as follows: Original Plan: [Copy the provided Planner Agent&apos;s plan here] Feedback: [Your detailed feedback to improve the plan here] Now, output your response below: Prompt for Refiner Agent: You are a Refiner Agent to provide a refined step-by-step plan for solving the given question. Question: {question} You are provided with: (1) latent-format information: a previous plan with feedback (2) text-format information: the input question you need to solve. Based on the input, write a refined and improved plan to solve the question. Make sure your output plan is correct and concise. Now, output your refined plan below: Prompt for Solver Agent: You are a helpful assistant. You are provided with latent information for reference and a target question to solve. Target Question: {question} The latent information might contain irrelevant contents. Ignore it if it is not helpful for solving the target question reason step-by-step and put the final answer inside \\boxed{YOUR FINAL ANSWER}. Your final answer must be selected from A,B,C,D. For example \\boxed{A}. Do not add any other contents inside the box. Question: {question} Your response: Hierarchical LatentMAS prompts for python coding tasks (MBPP-Plus, HumanEval-Plus</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b94\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">You must put all python code as self-contained Python function in markdown code blocks. For example &apos;&apos;&apos;python import math def add(a, b): return a + b&apos;&apos;&apos;. Do not add any other contents inside the markdown code block. Question: {question} Your response: Prompt for Science Agent: You are a science agent. Given the input question, reason step by step and provide an efficient and self-contained Python function that solves the following problem in a markdown code block. You must put all python code as self-contained Python function in markdown code blocks. For example &apos;&apos;&apos;python import math def add(a, b): return a + b&apos;&apos;&apos;. Do not add any other contents inside the markdown code block. Question: {question} Your response: Prompt for Code Agent: You are a code agent. Given the input question, reason step by step and provide an efficient and self-contained Python function that solves the following problem in a markdown code block. You must put all python code as self-contained Python function in markdown code blocks. For example &apos;&apos;&apos;python import math def add(a, b): return a + b&apos;&apos;&apos;. Do not add any other contents inside the markdown code block. Question: {question} Your response: Prompt for Task Summarizer Agent: You are a task summarizer. Given the input question and responses from previous agents as reference, reason step by step and provide an efficient and self-contained Python function that solves the following problem in a markdown code block. You must put all python code as self-contained Python function in markdown code blocks. For example</title>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Prompt for Math Agent: You are a math agent</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>System Prompt for All Agents: You are Qwen Given the input question, reason step by step and provide an efficient and self-contained Python function that solves the following problem in a markdown code block python import needed library def FUNC NAME(a, b): return a + b&apos;&apos;&apos;. Do not add any other contents inside the markdown code block. Input Question: {question} Your response</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n\t\t\t\t</listBibl>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</back>\n\t</text>\n</TEI>\n","pdf_hash":"10a9d1d141cfac51720abcd476d200f275db54d5ff3c74ec86a6f65341418ca2"}